|~ `::shape`, the kind of the shape `shape` answers, and the laws
   declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSPTH#shape]. ~|

:shape
  |~~ A shape is the structure of a value beneath its tags, which `shape`
      answers under `::shape`: the kind of each atom, as `type` answers
      it, a part under a tag standing as its tag, which tells of itself on
      its page; each map with its keys, `{}` an empty one; each vector one
      element whose shape holds of all of them, `[E]`, `[]` an empty one,
      records that share a key merged into one; each set `#[E]`, `#[]` an
      empty one; a tuple, `[A B]`, where vectors of one length part index
      by index; the kinds where parts part, `#[::number ::string]`; and the
      marks over a part, `::absent`, `::nullable` and `::each`. A shape is
      read as every value is: a path reads it beneath the tags over each
      part it meets, its marks among them, a list by its one element, a
      tuple by its indices and a fold by the key it shows, so a part read
      beneath a mark is answered without the mark, which stands over the
      part above it,
      `[{:author {:login "a"}} {:author null}] | shape | get /0/author/login`
      answering `::string` under a `::nullable` author. The shape of a part
      of the data is the shape of that part, `get /items | map /assignee | shape`,
      and its size, a sample and the share of its kinds are asked of the
      data, by `count`, `get /0` and `groupBy ~(type) | map ~count`.
      ::link~(::any/shape | doc) ::link~(::absent | doc)
      ::link~(::nullable | doc) ::link~(::each | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :isWhatShapeAnswers
        |~~ A shape is what `shape` answers, under its tag. ~~|
        ~({:a 1} | shape | eq ::shape{:a ::number})
    | proves :readsAPartBeneathItsTag
        |~~ A path reads a part of a shape beneath its tag, as it reads
            every value.
        ~~|
        ~({:a {:b 1}} | shape | get /a/b | eq ::number)
    | proves :opensASetAsItOpensAVector
        |~~ A set opens as a vector does, one element for all of them. ~~|
        ~({:s #[1 2]} | shape | eq ::shape{:s #[::number]})
